letters for OS-9/68000======================ORIG holds comp.sources.unix volume 25, Letter Invaders 2.1, as posted.The files beside it build the OS-9 program.What changed, and why:  config.h     Under OSK the words come from /dd/GAMES/words, the word list               the disk's other word games use, and the high scores are               kept in /dd/GAMES/LETTERS/letters.high.  That file ships               empty; ORIG/letters.high is the post's, with its players'               names.  kinput.c     The keyboard was set up with termio or sgtty ioctls and read               without blocking.  Under OSK setterm() turns off echo and               the end-of-file key with _gs_opt()/_ss_opt(), and               key_pressed() reads a key only when _gs_rdy() says one is               waiting.  SIGTERM is 15 where signal.h does not name it.  kinput.h     Microware's curses library, which every build here links,               has a setterm() of its own, so under OSK the program's is               letters_setterm.  term.c       No termio.h.  Microware's termlib defines BC and UP and names               the pad character PC_, so under OSK term.c declares them               instead of defining them.  usleep.c     select() is not here; under OSK usleep() is tsleep() with the               high bit set, which counts in 256ths of a second.  It never               asks for less than 4: measured under os9exec, a sleep of 1 or               2 256ths returns at once and 4 is one 100 Hz tick, and the               10 ms pause between key polls rounded to 2 let every word               fall the whole screen without waiting.  highscore.c  The player's name comes from $USER, since there is no               password file to ask; "nobody" if it is unset.  recipe       -DNOJOB (no job control), -Drandom=rand -Dsrandom=srand.letters.c, word.c, term.h and terms.h build unchanged.Measured: words appear at the top and fall at a playable pace (twoscreens taken four seconds apart differ); with no word typed the gameends in about twelve seconds, as its short words drop three lines a step,and prints the score table and its final line.Build: cc letters.c highscore.c kinput.c term.c word.c usleep.c -DOSK          -DNOJOB -Drandom=rand -Dsrandom=srand -l=termlib.l